        "BIO": "Dr. Syed Zohaib Hassan is an Assistant Professor of Practice in the Department of Civil Engineering at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley. He earned his Ph.D. in Civil Engineering from the University of Central Florida, where he also served as a Postdoctoral Scholar. His teaching interests include numerical methods, civil engineering materials, geotechnical engineering, geospatial technologies, and data-driven engineering analysis.<br><br>Dr. Hassan's research focuses on integrating unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), remote sensing, geospatial analytics, and artificial intelligence to address challenges in civil and environmental engineering. His work integrates LiDAR, photogrammetry, thermal and multispectral imaging, computer vision, machine learning, and geographic information systems (GIS) to develop innovative solutions for infrastructure assessment, environmental monitoring, precision agriculture, and smart sensing systems.<br><br>Dr. Hassan is passionate about experiential learning and strives to connect engineering theory with real-world applications through hands-on projects, undergraduate research, and the integration of emerging technologies into civil engineering education. His goal is to prepare students with the technical knowledge and practical skills needed to address contemporary challenges in civil and environmental engineering.",
